    "modified": true,
    "modifications": "2 real Key West street paths stitched through the OSM graph, heading Gaussian-smoothed, positions re-integrated from heading, then pinned back onto the real junctions (largest drift closed 40.4 m, spread back along each line), resampled at 2 m with curvature from the sampled positions; land elevation from 3DEP low-pass filtered, bridge decks synthesized (3DEP is bare earth); lanes simplified to the configured cross-section; junction connector roads synthesized (a turn, a straight and a turn)"
  },
  "meta": {
    "status": "live",
    "notes": "A real-road network (run W-S; interview, 2026-10-02: map-based networks, multi-lane highways, junction choices): the Overseas Highway (US 1) four lanes wide over Stock Island and Cow Key Channel into Key West, then South Roosevelt Boulevard along Smathers Beach, Bertha Street and Atlantic Boulevard to Higgs Beach; North Roosevelt Boulevard leaves at the Triangle and comes back down Truman Avenue and White Street, about the same distance. Its own frame origin, since it never shares a scene with keys-m1. Junction pieces and connector roads are synthesized; the lines are pinned to the real junctions (closure)."
  }
